## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card which flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;          /* width of the card */
  height: 200px;         /* height of the card */
  perspective: 1000px;   /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  margin: 50px auto;     /* center horizontally */
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  The card itself ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
}

/* Hover triggers the flip */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face */
.card-front {
  background: #4CAF50;          /* green background */
  color: white;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
}

/* Back face */
.card-back {
  background: #2196F3;          /* blue background */
  color: white;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* start rotated so it becomes visible after flip */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | CSS property |
|------|--------------|--------------|
| 1 | The wrapper (`.card-wrapper`) sets a `perspective` so the 3D rotation looks realistic. | `perspective: 1000px;` |
| 2 | The `.card` element is the rotating container. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3D space. | `transform-style: preserve-3d;` |
| 3 | On hover, the card is rotated 180° around the Y‑axis. | `transform: rotateY(180deg);` |
| 4 | Each face (`.card-face`) has `backface-visibility: hidden` so the hidden side isn’t shown. The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so it appears correctly after the flip. | `backface-visibility: hidden;` / `transform: rotateY(180deg);` |

Feel free to replace the colors, text, or add more content inside the faces. The same technique works for X‑axis flips (`rotateX`) or 3‑D rotations (`rotate3d`). Enjoy!
